# Agentic Memory 6-Tier Cognitive Architecture & Doyle's TMS
(Assimilated from Verace-Pvt-Ltd/agentic-memory)

## 1. 6-Tier Memory Taxonomy
- **Sensory Memory (Ring Buffer, N=100)**: Instant triage of raw event streams, calculating saliency score. RTT < 0.2ms via Write-Ahead Memory Buffer (WAMB).
- **Working Memory (Bounded Attention Window)**: Active multi-turn context (up to 8k tokens) tracking current goal, constraints, and chronological observations.
- **Episodic Memory (Task Trajectories)**: Structured traces (goal, tool calls, outcomes, reward score). Causality edges (`cause_of`, `led_to`).
- **Semantic Memory (SPO Triplet Knowledge Graph)**: Subject-Predicate-Object triples with vector embeddings and Personalized PageRank (PPR) spreading activation.
- **Long-Term Memory (Persistent TMS Facts)**: Doyle's Truth Maintenance System with bitemporal validities (`valid_from`, `valid_until`, `defeated_by_id`).
- **Procedural Memory (Tool Sequences & Skills)**: Workflows with tracking of `success_count`, `failure_count`, and `avg_latency_ms`.

## 2. Mathematical Formulations & Algorithms

### 2.1 Ebbinghaus Retrievability with Spaced Retrieval Reinforcement
$$R(t) = \exp\left( -\frac{\Delta t}{T_{\text{half}} \times (1 + 0.25 \times n_{\text{retrievals}})} \right)$$
- If item is pinned (`is_pinned=True`) or $\text{importance} \ge 0.95$, retrievability is pinned to $R(t) \equiv 1.0$.
- Pruning/consolidation candidates are flagged when $R(t) < \theta_{\text{evict}}$.

### 2.2 Fused Multi-Factor Ranking
$$S_{\text{final}} = w_{\text{sim}} \cdot S_{\text{vector}} + w_{\text{rec}} \cdot R(t) + w_{\text{imp}} \cdot I + w_{\text{trust}} \cdot T_{\text{discount}}$$
- Trust levels: `SYSTEM (1.0)`, `USER (0.95)`, `TOOL_OUTPUT (0.85)`, `AGENT_INFERRED (0.70)`, `EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED (0.40)`.

### 2.3 Doyle's Truth Maintenance (Non-Destructive Belief Revision)
When a contradicting fact $F_{\text{new}}$ defeats $F_{\text{old}}$:
- $F_{\text{old}}.\text{is\_active} \leftarrow \text{False}$
- $F_{\text{old}}.\text{defeated\_by\_id} \leftarrow F_{\text{new}}.\text{id}$
- $F_{\text{old}}.\text{valid\_until} \leftarrow t_{\text{now}}$
Queries with $t < t_{\text{now}}$ reconstruct exact historical beliefs without destructive overwrites.

### 2.4 Prompt Fencing & Injection Protection
All memory items escape XML/HTML brackets (`<` -> `&lt;`, `>` -> `&gt;`) and are fenced inside strict contextual blocks before prompt injection.
